---
title: Momofuku Milk Bar Corn Cookies
description: Momofuku Milk Bar's chewy corn cookies, made with freeze-dried corn powder.
tags: [cookies, baking]
course: dessert
author: Christina Tosi
source: Momofuku Milk Bar
yield: 13-15%cookies
time: 2h15m
---

Combine the @butter{225%g}(16 tbsp, at room temperature) and @sugar{300%g}(1 1/2 cups) in the bowl of a #stand mixer{} fitted with the paddle attachment and cream together on medium-high for ~cream{2-3%minutes}.

Scrape down the sides of the bowl, add the @egg{1}, and beat for ~beat{7-8%minutes}.

Reduce the mixer speed to low and add the @flour{225%g}(1 1/3 cups), @corn flour{45%g}(1/4 cup), @freeze-dried corn powder{65%g}(2/3 cup), @baking powder{3/4%tsp}(3 g), @baking soda{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g), and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}(6 g). Mix just until the dough comes together, no longer than ~mix{1%minute}. Scrape down the sides of the bowl.

> The chefs at Milk Bar make freeze-dried corn powder by grinding freeze-dried corn. You can find freeze-dried corn at Whole Foods, Amazon.com, or JustTomatoes.com. Store leftover powder in an airtight container so it won't absorb moisture.

Using a 2 3/4-ounce #ice cream scoop{} (or a 1/3-cup measure), portion out the dough onto a parchment-lined #sheet pan{}.

Pat the tops of the cookie dough domes flat.

Wrap the sheet pan tightly in #plastic wrap{} and refrigerate for at least ~chill{1%hour}, or up to 1 week (do not bake your cookies from room temperature — they will not bake properly).

Heat the oven to 350°F (175°C).

Arrange the chilled dough a minimum of 4 inches apart on parchment- or Silpat-lined sheet pans. Bake for ~bake{18%minutes}. The cookies will puff, crackle, and spread. After 18 minutes, they should be faintly browned on the edges yet still bright yellow in the center; give them an extra ~bake{1%minute} if not.

Cool the cookies completely on the sheet pans before transferring to a plate or to an #airtight container{} for storage.

> At room temperature, the cookies will keep fresh for 5 days; in the freezer, they will keep for 1 month.
